# Kirukal v2 — Interactive Diary Walkthrough

## What Was Built

A complete rework of Kirukal from a canvas editor into a **narrative interactive diary** where your hand-drawn sketches connect to real work.

---

## Git Branches

| Branch | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `previous` | Your original canvas editor (fully preserved) |
| `v2-interactive-diary` | All new work lives here |

---

## New Pages

| Route | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `/` | New landing page with diary + editor CTAs |
| `/diary` | Main interactive diary view |
| `/editor` | Original editor (unchanged) |
| `/api/og-preview` | Server-side OG link metadata fetcher |

---

## Diary Features

### 📖 Two Layout Modes
- **Single:** Diary page centered, sketches on left, links/videos on right
- **Double:** Open-notebook book spread — left page shows scanned photo, right page shows diary text

### 📸 Page Scanner (AI-powered, offline)
Click **Scan Page** to:
1. **Camera** or **file upload** a physical diary page
2. AI detects page edges (Canny edge detection via OpenCV.js)
3. Drag 4 corner handles to fine-tune the crop
4. AI detects individual sketch components (contour grouping)
5. Review each detected sketch — approve, rename, or reject
6. Everything saves to Supabase automatically

### ✨ Hover Connections
- Diary text phrases can be linked to media items
- Hover a linked phrase → floating media preview popup appears
- Animated SVG arcs draw between the text and its linked media card

---

## Setup Required

### 1. Create Supabase Project (Free)
1. Go to [supabase.com](https://supabase.com) → **New Project** (free tier)
2. Go to **SQL Editor** → paste the contents of [supabase/schema.sql](file:///c:/Users/arunk/KIRUKULAM/kirukals/supabase/schema.sql) → **Run**
3. Go to **Storage** → Create two buckets:
   - `diary-pages` (Public)
   - `sketch-components` (Public)
4. Go to **Settings → API** → copy `Project URL` and `anon key`

### 2. Configure Environment
```bash
# Rename the example file
cp .env.local.example .env.local
```
Then edit `.env.local`:
```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
```

### 3. Add OpenCV.js (for page scanning)
OpenCV.js is loaded from local `/opencv.js`. Download it once:
```
https://docs.opencv.org/4.10.0/opencv.js → save to /public/opencv.js
```
Or it will attempt to load from `public/opencv.js` — the first load may fail gracefully if not present.

### 4. Run
```bash
npm run dev
```

